        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Technical review: Document TRANSIENT_ATTACHMENT usage]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43773</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43773"/>
        <updated>2026-04-13T17:55:35.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Chrome 146 adds support for the <code class="notranslate">TRANSIENT_ATTACHMENT</code> <code class="notranslate">GPUTextureUsage</code>; see <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5562829589577728" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5562829589577728</a>, and also see <a href="https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-146#transient_attachments" rel="nofollow">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-146#transient_attachments</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds documentation for the new usage type.</p>

