<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Chrome has added support for two features that allow sites to size fonts in proportion to the operating system/browser text scale settings:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>The <code class="notranslate">&lt;meta name="text-scale" content="..." /&gt;</code> element, which was added in Chrome 146, and works across Desktop and Mobile platforms. See <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5112244702674944" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5112244702674944</a>.</li>
<li>The <code class="notranslate">preferred-text-scale</code> <code class="notranslate">env()</code> variable, which was added in Chrome 138. This only really works in Android,</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">This PR documents both of these features.</p>

